&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you will work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our New York City office (in the Financial District). You must be willing to work in the office 3 days per week on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own KPIs and dashboards end-to-end.&lt;/strong&gt; Build, maintain, and govern key KPIs and dashboards across business domains, managing the full lifecycle of analytics projects from scoping to delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a thought partner on measurement.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with stakeholders to define how success is measured across Garner&#39;s products and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable data pipelines.&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with the data engineering team to create maintainable pipelines that power reliable reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop deep domain expertise.&lt;/strong&gt; Build a strong understanding of your analytical domain so you can independently drive meaningful insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close reporting gaps.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify where coverage is missing and proactively develop new dashboards and insights to fill them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar on data practices.&lt;/strong&gt; Advocate for best practices in visualization, documentation, metric consistency, and stakeholder communication across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Answer high-stakes, ambiguous questions.&lt;/strong&gt; Run deep-dive investigations into complex business problems — the kind of analysis leadership uses to make strategic calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
