&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; of experience &lt;/strong&gt;in Data Analytics, Business Intelligence, or a similar data-centric role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional translation.&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to translate ambiguous business questions into data-driven solutions and to work effectively with non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy and ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working independently and owning reporting projects end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation mindset.&lt;/strong&gt; Attention to detail with a bias toward automation and scalability over one-off work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Nativity.&lt;/strong&gt; Comfort with and excitement about building analytics, building dashboards, and validating results by harnessing the power of AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Making data accessible&lt;/strong&gt;. A track record of getting stakeholders trustworthy, self-serve access to the information they need. Experience with a BI/visualization tool (Looker, Tableau, Power BI, or similar) helps — but the outcome matters more than the specific tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern data stack. &lt;/strong&gt;Hands-on with Snowflake (or a comparable cloud warehouse) and SQL at scale; experience with dbt strongly preferred — you&#39;ll partner with Data Management in governed pipelines, not just consume their outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to be part of a high-performing, mission-driven team that operates with intense urgency, a strong sense of individual accountability, and a commitment to authentic feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to join a fast-growing company in a transformative role, helping shape the future of healthcare.&lt;/p&gt;
