&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Associate, Marketing Operations to own the operational engine behind Garner’s demand generation motion. You will run day-to-day campaign operations, deliver marketing reporting and analysis, and keep lead data flowing to sales with speed and fidelity. This is an automation-first role: you will use AI tools to continuously convert manual work into monitored, hands-free processes, so the role gets more leveraged as you build. This role reports to the Director of Marketing Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you will work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our New York City office (in the Financial District). You must be willing to work in the office 3 days per week on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own campaign operations end-to-end, including campaign enrollment, list processing, tracking setup, and CRM data hygiene, ensuring every campaign is accurately tracked and attribution is preserved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the marketing ops request queue, triaging and delivering requests within SLA and escalating only what requires systems-level judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools and automation to convert repetitive campaign ops and request work into hands-free, monitored processes, measured by declining manual effort per campaign&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver marketing reporting and analysis, maintaining and automating the reporting library (recurring refreshes and event, webinar, and email performance reports) and executing one-off data pulls and analyses as needs arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day lead routing operations, monitoring flow health, resolving routing exceptions, and maintaining speed-to-lead as routing logic and data sources evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring to the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–3 years of experience in marketing operations, revenue operations, or a related operational role, preferably at a B2B organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on HubSpot experience (workflows, forms, segmentation); Salesforce familiarity is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An automation-first mindset: you’re comfortable with detail-oriented execution, and you’re routinely asking how a process could be made repeatable or hands-free&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI tools (e.g., Claude) applied to real workflows, or strong motivation to build it fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data comfort: confident building reports and working in spreadsheets; SQL or Python exposure is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter mindset toward understanding, documenting, and navigating new systems&lt;/li&gt;
