&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Own how member activation and engagement are measured end-to-end (e.g., Looker dashboards). Define, build, and maintain the KPIs, metric definitions, performance reports, and dashboards Growth Marketing runs on — funnel and lifecycle metrics, email/SMS campaign activity, channel efficiency, operational health, and KPI target setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; engagement analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Bridge marketing activity to member behavior in the Garner app so the team can optimize communications over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop and execute on the Growth Marketing team’s A/B testing program and performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data governance:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Build our data foundation alongside Data Management &amp;amp; Engineering, Reporting &amp;amp; Business Intelligence, Growth Product to ensure our data is analysis-ready and trustworthy. Build workflows, documentation, QA practices, and tooling that ensure our metrics are standardized across systems and campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems &amp;amp; technology stack:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Uplevel our data sophistication by designing and building at the systems level, leveraging AI in order to maximize scale and leverage.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
